 ```
 
+#### Max Consecutive Losses
+
+`MaxConsecutiveLosses` looks at trades for a pair within `lookback_period` in minutes (or in candles when using `lookback_period_candles`), starting from the most recently closed trade and walking backwards.
+If `trade_limit` or more of these trades in a row resulted in a loss (profit below `required_profit`, which defaults to 0.0), that pair will be locked for `stop_duration` in minutes (or in candles when using `stop_duration_candles`, or until the set time when using `unlock_at`). The streak is broken - and no lock will be applied - as soon as a winning trade is encountered.
+
+This applies across all pairs (bot-wide), unless `only_per_pair` is set to true, which will then only look at one pair at a time - locking a pair after its own losing streak without affecting other pairs.
+
+Similarly, this protection will by default look at all trades (long and short). For futures bots, setting `only_per_side` will make the bot only consider one side, and will then only lock this one side, allowing for example shorts to continue after a series of long losses.
+
+The below example stops trading for all pairs for 12 candles after 4 losing trades occurred in a row (bot-wide) within the last 24 candles.
+
+``` python
+@property
+def protections(self):
+    return [
+        {
+            "method": "MaxConsecutiveLosses",
+            "lookback_period_candles": 24,
+            "trade_limit": 4,
+            "stop_duration_candles": 12,
+            "required_profit": 0.0,
+            "only_per_pair": False,
+            "only_per_side": False
+        }
+    ]
+```
+
+To instead only lock the pair that had the losing streak (leaving all other pairs untouched), set `only_per_pair` to `True`:
+
+``` python
+@property
+def protections(self):
+    return [
+        {
+            "method": "MaxConsecutiveLosses",
+            "lookback_period_candles": 24,
+            "trade_limit": 3,
+            "stop_duration_candles": 12,
+            "only_per_pair": True
+        }
+    ]
+```
+
 #### Cooldown Period
 
 `CooldownPeriod` locks a pair for `stop_duration` in minutes (or in candles when using `stop_duration_candles`, or until the set time when using `unlock_at`) after exiting, avoiding a re-entry for this pair for `stop_duration` minutes.
